  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1036 AM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nCOOL AND DRY THROUGH THE WEEKEND: \n\nWith high pressure driving the forecast, sunny days, clear \nnights, and dry conditons continue through the weekend. A Freeze\nWarning remains in effect tonight for parts of northwest \nColorado and CO Zone 23 in southwest Colorado with another night\nof sub-freezing temperatures expected. Most locations within \nthe Freeze Warning also saw a hard freeze last night.\n\nOtherwise, seasonable to seasonably cool daytime temperatures \nhighlight the forecast through the weekend. \n\nUNSETTLED WEATHER RETURNS NEXT WEEK:\n\nThe next chance for impactful weather comes next week as a low \npressure system traverses the West. Ahead of this system, \nsouthwesterly flow will begin to direct moisture towards the \nregion as early as Monday. As a result, isolated convection is \npossible over the southern Mountains early in the week. By mid- \nweek, an uptick in synoptic forcing could increase the coverage \nof showers and storms across the region. It's too early to pin \ndown the potential hazards associated with this system, but \nexpect increasingly unsettled weather as the week progresses.",
